{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2b3bb860-30be-4beb-a6f3-26a3a45f4f31","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Newton's second law connects the net force on an object to its acceleration.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"law","region":"A1","content":"Newton's second law"},{"op":"equation","id":"n2","region":"A2","latex":"\\sum \\vec{F}=m\\vec{a}"},{"op":"sketch","id":"block","region":"right","strokes":[[[0.35,0.55],[0.65,0.55],[0.65,0.75],[0.35,0.75],[0.35,0.55]]]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2b3bb860-30be-4beb-a6f3-26a3a45f4f31","step":{"id":"s2","script":"For a block on a horizontal surface, gravity and the normal force balance vertically.","ops":[{"op":"sketch","id":"gravity","region":"right","strokes":[[[0.5,0.55],[0.5,0.9]],[[0.47,0.86],[0.5,0.9],[0.53,0.86]],[[0.5,0.55],[0.5,0.3]],[[0.47,0.34],[0.5,0.3],[0.53,0.34]]]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"If vertical acceleration is zero, what must be true about the vertical forces?","expected_gist":"They balance; net vertical force is zero."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2b3bb860-30be-4beb-a6f3-26a3a45f4f31","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A horizontal push creates the net force, so the block accelerates in the push direction.","ops":[{"op":"sketch","id":"push","region":"right","strokes":[[[0.15,0.65],[0.35,0.65]],[[0.29,0.61],[0.35,0.65],[0.29,0.69]],[[0.65,0.65],[0.85,0.65]],[[0.81,0.61],[0.85,0.65],[0.81,0.69]]]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"2b3bb860-30be-4beb-a6f3-26a3a45f4f31","step":{"id":"s4","script":"After adding forces as vectors, solve the horizontal equation for acceleration.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"horizontal","anchor":{"el":"n2","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\sum F_x=ma_x\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad a_x=\\frac{\\sum F_x}{m}"},{"op":"text","id":"conclusion","anchor":{"el":"horizontal","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"Net force determines acceleration"}],"checkpoint":null}}
